                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "I need a full audit of the tool execution pipeline. Start with how cancel tokens are created and propagated - I think they are being shared across concurrent calls, which is causing the message drop we saw yesterday. Once that is clear, trace how errors bubble up from tool results: right now a single MCP failure takes down the entire session instead of being isolated at the tool boundary.\n\nThe streaming preview logic in event-controller.ts has a race condition when partial JSON arrives before the tool call object closes.  The bash tool preview disappears mid-stream and only re-appears at the end. Check whether partialJson needs to flow through the transcript rebuild path as well as the live path. \n\nAlso, the TUI differential renderer drops entire rows when a line contains a tab character. replaceTabs() is not being called on the error message path, only the success path. Fix it and add a note to the render checklist in AGENTS.md.",
