    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "yNrnj",
      "x": 7353,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "note1",
      "width": 320,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Attention Queue — the colored bar above the session tree. Rows are sessions waiting for user input. Next! hotkey / button walks a cursor through the queue with wraparound; the 'current' row is visually stronger. Pressing Next! does NOT remove rows; only sending a message or 'done for now' (hover check button) does."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "PruHh",
      "x": 7695,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "note2",
      "width": 320,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Next! button color mirrors the NEXT queue item (the one pressing it would warp you to). Here the current row is danger-pi (love) and the next row is api-server (iris), so the button is iris. When the queue is empty, the button switches to a 'Waiting...' state (no color) and the next session that needs input auto-warps you."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "20FXj",
      "x": 8036,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "note3",
      "width": 320,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "'Done for now' check button appears on hover per row. Removes the session from the queue ephemerally; if the same session later enters a waiting state, it re-enters the queue normally. Not a persistent mute."
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Kl0jX",
      "x": 6982,
      "y": 800,
      "name": "Recap Callout (in context)",
      "width": 1080,
      "fill": "$--base",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "padding": 40,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "d7sus",
          "name": "component/Recap Callout",
          "reusable": true,
          "width": 1000,
          "fill": "$--accent-bg",
          "cornerRadius": [
            0,
            "$--radius-lg",
            "$--radius-lg",
            0
          ],
          "stroke": {
            "align": "inside",
            "thickness": {
              "left": 3
            },
            "fill": "$--accent"
          },
          "layout": "vertical",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "WQnss",
              "name": "inner",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 14,
              "padding": [
                24,
                32
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "U7MMX",
                  "name": "header",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "gap": 10,
                  "alignItems": "center",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "icon_font",
                      "id": "crvaa",
                      "name": "recapIcon",
                      "width": 14,
                      "height": 14,
                      "iconFontName": "bookmark",
                      "iconFontFamily": "lucide",
                      "fill": "$--accent"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "8SQoD",
                      "name": "recapLabel",
                      "fill": "$--accent",
                      "content": "WHERE YOU LEFT OFF",
                      "fontFamily": "$--font-mono",
                      "fontSize": "$--font-size-caption",
                      "fontWeight": "600",
                      "letterSpacing": 1.2
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "mi5Wq",
                      "name": "recapDot",
                      "fill": "$--muted",
                      "content": "·",
                      "fontFamily": "$--font-mono",
                      "fontSize": "$--font-size-caption",
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "X7mPS",
                      "name": "recapTime",
                      "fill": "$--muted",
                      "content": "52 min ago",
                      "fontFamily": "$--font-mono",
                      "fontSize": "$--font-size-caption",
                      "fontWeight": "500",
                      "letterSpacing": 0.5
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HA2bF",
                  "name": "recapBody",
                  "fill": "$--text",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "We were mid-way through scaffolding the OAuth token store. The agent finished wiring up the refresh token rotation logic and is now waiting for your call on how to handle the edge case where a refresh token is used twice in rapid succession — replay attack or legitimate race?\n\nBefore you left, you'd discussed three possible approaches: (1) fail both requests and force re-authentication, (2) honor the first request and invalidate the second, or (3) use a short grace window to treat both as the same logical refresh. The agent drafted a proof-of-concept for approach (2) but flagged that it needs your review because it touches the session invalidation path, which has implications for the mobile client's reconnect logic.\n\nAlso worth knowing: the test suite was updated to include a new integration test for the rotation flow, but it's currently skipped pending your decision on the edge case above. The code is on branch feat/auth-rewrite and has not yet been pushed.",
                  "lineHeight": "$--line-height-reading",
                  "fontFamily": "$--font-serif",
                  "fontSize": "$--font-size-body-lg",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
